Further reduced REST API query counts at `?depth>=1` for cable-connected models — the cable-peer and connected-endpoint prefetches now offer an enriched flavor (used automatically by the REST API at depth>=1) whose inner querysets prefetch each termination type's natural-key chains, so nested peer representations resolve their `natural_slug` without per-peer queries. A 100-row Circuits list at depth=2 dropped from ~1,100 to ~340 queries; Interfaces at depth=1 from 125 to 78. UI table rendering keeps the existing lean prefetches.
